Dual License
============

This repository contains two categories of content, licensed differently:

1. **Code** (everything under `benchmarks/`, `patches/*.py` if any, and any other
   `.py` / script / software file in this repository) is licensed under the
   **MIT License** (full text below).

2. **Paper / written content** (everything under `paper/`, including the `.tex`
   source and the compiled `.pdf`, plus any other prose documentation intended as
   the research narrative rather than software) is licensed under
   **Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0)**.

If it is unclear which license applies to a given file, check the directory it
lives in first (`benchmarks/` = MIT, `paper/` = CC-BY-4.0); `docs/` and
`environment/` files default to CC-BY-4.0 unless they are executable scripts, in
which case MIT applies.

